      "exposure": "rare",
      "claim": "ruleDelta reads the working side of every changed declaration file straight from disk (os.ReadFile), while acdsl check loads rules only from FileUniverse (git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard). A branch in a gated/strict repo that untracks and ignores a declaration file therefore drops every rule in it from the gate while CheckPolicy reports zero removed rules. Sequence (2 commands, zero cost, deterministic, local gate): `git rm --cached acdsl/rules.acdsl` then `echo acdsl/rules.acdsl >> .git/info/exclude` (no tracked .gitignore edit needed). DiscoverRules no longer sees acdsl/rules.acdsl, so all central doctrine rules stop running; GitChangedFiles lists the path (diff-index reports it deleted vs base), ruleDelta's os.ReadFile still returns the unchanged bytes, workRules == baseRules, delta.removed is empty; surfaceDelta does not cover rules.acdsl. `acdsl check` exits 0 with the whole central rule set disabled, contradicting CheckPolicy's promise that strict/gated branches cannot remove rules off the base branch. Not a variant of the known rename-detection or base_ref entries: the file keeps its path and the base is resolved correctly.",
      "evidence": "Re-read internal/acdsl/policy.go:237-280 (ruleDelta: os.ReadFile at 248 regardless of tracked/ignored status; base via GitShowFile at 251), policy.go:31-36 (policySurface lists only policy.json, policy.schema.json, registry.json, evalgen.json), policy.go:368-374 (removed class judged only from ruleDelta), internal/acdsl/git.go:46-66 (GitChangedFiles = git diff --name-only base + ls-files --others --exclude-standard), cmd/acdsl/main.go:86 and 127-132 (rules come from DiscoverRules, policy delta from CheckPolicy), internal/acdsl/load.go:38-47 and run.go FileUniverse (ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard: an untracked ignored file is excluded). The two views diverge exactly for a file present on disk but neither indexed nor unignored. Probe not run: lane constraints forbid git writes outside the pin, so no scratch repo could be committed; reproduction sequence stated above for the refuter (newPolicyRepo fixture in policy_test.go + the two commands + CheckPolicy and DiscoverRules).",
      "fix": "In ruleDelta, take the working side only for paths in FileUniverse(ctx, root) — treat a changed path absent from the universe as deleted (no workLines entry) so its base rules land in delta.removed."
    }
  ],
